/*!
    \page vscodeext-how-create-qrc-files.html
    \previouspage vscodeext-how-tos.html
    \nextpage vscodeext-reference.html

    \ingroup vscodeext-how-to-cpp

    \title Create Qt resource collection files

    \l {The Qt Resource System} is a platform-independent mechanism for storing
    files in the application's executable. Use it if your application always
    needs a certain set of files (like icons, translation files, images), and
    you don't want to use system-specific means to package and locate these
    resources.

    You can create and edit Qt resource collection (\c .qrc) files.

    \section1 Create QRC files

    To create a new QRC file:

    \list 1
        \li Go to \uicontrol {Command Palette}, and then select
            \uicontrol {Qt: Create a new project or file}.
        \li In \uicontrol {File}, select \uicontrol {Qt resource file}.
            \image {vscodeext-create-new-qrc-file.webp} {Qt resource file selected in the New item view}
        \li In \uicontrol {Name}, enter a name for the file.
        \li In \uicontrol {Create in}, enter the path for the file.
        \li Select \uicontrol {Create} to create the file.
    \endlist

    \section1 Edit QRC files

    Add groups with different prefixes to structure the resources and avoid
    clashes between resource files that you add through different \c {.qrc}
    files in different libraries or plugins.

    Sometimes it is convenient to make a resource file available under a
    different path at runtime. .qrc files allow this by setting an \c {alias}
    attribute.

    To edit a QRC file:

    \list 1
        \li Open a \c {.qrc} file.
            \image {vscodeext-edit-qrc-file.webp} {Qt resource file open in the editor}
        \li Select \uicontrol {Files} to add files to the group.
        \li In \uicontrol {Alias}, set the path where the resource file is
            available at runtime.
        \li In \uicontrol {Prefix}, set a prefix to add to each local file name
            to get the name by which the file is known within the resource
            system.
        \li In \uicontrol {Language}, set a suitable locale string to select
            resources, such as translation files or icons, based on the user's
            locale.
    \endlist

    \sa {Tutorial: Qt Widgets application}, {Create Qt projects}
*/
